Um, where did you hear this?  Last I checked, my uncle flying with the Alaskan Air Patrol routinely had run-ins with MiG fighters.  Now, the AAP runs patrols over that nice little strait between Alaska and Russia (formerly the USSR).  We were on bad terms with the USSR, and yet would occasionally let them get over land before "escorting" them away.<br>
<br>
  Now, China has stated that they want to be a prefered trading partner.  That they want to be recognised as major partners in the international community.  Generally, that they want to be buddies because it's profitable.  And yet when we place a survalence plane (it's not a spy plane, it's not only impossible to hide but it actually runs on a regular schedual on a regular route which is not classified in any way) over international waters to make sure that they're not doing something stupid, it gets hit by one of their hot-dogging fighter jocks.  And with the speed and manuverability of your average fighter, that survalence plane flying in a steady straight line is effectivly a stationary object in a very big sky.  It's like you in a Porsche trying to tail a Honda Civic with a 2 ton trailer.  If anything, it takes effort to go that slow.<br>
<br>
  And bear in mind, China has done some stupid things before.  Things like placing missiles along the coast pointed at Japan and Taiwan.  These countries are recognised allies whom we have agreed to defend.  If that plane was closer to Japan than to China, but China still claimed the waters, who do they belong to?  Does China get 200 miles offshore and the entire "first island chain" (Japan, Taiwan, and the Phillipeans) like they claim, just because they say so?  If we start letting every country in the world set its own standards, there are going to be some serious conflicts over who owns what.  US airspace extends 7 miles from our shores.  We may patrol beyond this, but that is far different from claiming ownership.  China is more than welcome to patrol international airspace, and they have done so.  But if they're going to start claiming everything that someone from the Manchu dyansty ever laid eyes on, they can kiss my ass.<br>
